  // an electropermanent cargo magnet: a pad under a pylon. A clamp ("iman": it takes what is
  // under it as it is) with its machine (the pulses that switch it). It takes everything under
  // its face (the middle of each thing within a hand of the pad's edge, its top against the
  // pad), the nearest first, up to its rated load ("carga", kg: a lifting magnet is rated by
  // mass; a pad this size lifts 2.5 t at 3:1); what would take it past that it leaves, and
  // says so (<id>.sobrecarga). <id>.masa: what it holds weighs
